Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Skip unchanged unlimited bandwidth updates

systemd writes "max 100000" to cpu.max of every unit with the cpu
controller.  tg_set_cfs_bandwidth() then takes the runqueue lock of every
online CPU to rewrite runtime_enabled and runtime_remaining, although
nothing changes.

Return early when the bandwidth stays unlimited with the same period and
burst.
---
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -9582,6 +9582,10 @@ static int tg_set_cfs_bandwidth(struct task_group *tg,
 	ret = __cfs_schedulable(tg, period, quota);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	if (quota == RUNTIME_INF && cfs_b->quota == RUNTIME_INF &&
+	    ktime_to_ns(cfs_b->period) == period && cfs_b->burst == burst)
+		return 0;
 
 	runtime_enabled = quota != RUNTIME_INF;
 	runtime_was_enabled = cfs_b->quota != RUNTIME_INF;
